`DatasetRolling.construct` first imports `Dataset`, normalizes `keep_attrs`, skips the `window_dim is None` block because the test passes `window_dim="win"`, then computes `window_dims` and `strides`. It initializes `dataset` and loops over `self.obj.data_vars.items()`: for `"signal"` the rolling dimension `"x"` is present, so it builds `dims`, `wi`, and `st`, calls the nested `DataArrayRolling.construct`, then clears attrs because `keep_attrs` is false; for `"meta"` no rolling dimension is present, so it copies the array and also clears attrs. After the loop it strides coordinates with `isel(...).coords`, sets `attrs` to `{}` because `keep_attrs` is false, and returns `Dataset(dataset, coords=coords, attrs=attrs)`.

